    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-18T21:17:12+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-18T21:17:12+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T10:47:12Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-18T10:47:12Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system and associated trough over Western Australia move over western South Australia this evening and broadly across the state during Thursday, clearing to the east early Friday. A high pressure system will then move across southern SA from Friday, before a trough and cold front move across the west late Saturday and across the rest of SA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW006" description="Riverland" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-18T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Light winds.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the evening. Winds easterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northerly 15 to 25 km/h in the middle of the day then tending east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 19 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the morning then becoming southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 17 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 13 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon. Winds northerly 20 to 30 km/h shifting west to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to the low 20s with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
